{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Take from them, etc.</b> The verse's saying <b>from them</b> teaches that the offerings were still in the possession of those who brought them and had not yet entered the possession of Moses. The reason of Moses was that since he had not been commanded that they should load the Tabernacle on the wagons, he did not wish to accept them — for why are they fitting? But the princes reasoned in their own minds that the planks and the sockets are a heavy load that requires wagons, and the mind of the Holy One, blessed be He, concurred."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:29.434912555Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}